/P 201 0 R
/E (We are pleased to advise that the church repairs are moving forward, with work expected to commence in August. While we hope there will be minimal disruption to Masses and parish activities, there may be occasions when changes are necessary. If so, please check our parish website and weekly bulletin for updates.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
41 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Our church repairs fundraising campaign continues to make wonderful progress. Thanks to the generosity of our parish community, we have now raised $119,695 towards our $150,000 goal. The response has been both humbling and inspiring, and we sincerely thank everyone who has contributed. Your generosity is helping preserve our church for future generations.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
42 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (We thank the Year 5 students from St Thomas' School for leading the Saturday evening Mass on 13 June. It was a joy to witness the reverence and enthusiasm with which they embraced their ministries. Thank you also to the teachers and families who supported them.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
43 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Congratulations to our Year 4 students from St Thomas' School who celebrated their First Holy Communion in June. We pray this special sacrament will deepen their relationship with Christ and strengthen them on their faith journey. We also thank their families, teachers and sacramental team for their support.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
44 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (On 28 June, our parish celebrated the Festival of St Vincent, where new members of the St Vincent de Paul Society were commissioned into their ministry. Following Mass, parishioners gathered for morning tea with our local St Vincent de Paul members. We thank all members of the Society for their compassionate service and wish the new members every blessing.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
